---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HorizontalCard from "../components/HorizontalCard.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title = "Projects" sideBarActiveItemID="projects">
  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5">Machine Learning</div>
  </div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="A Unifying Post-Processing Framework for Multi-Objective Learn-to-Defer Problems"
    img="/uni.webp"
    desc="This paper introduces a unifying framework for constrained optimization problems, mainly for classification and learn-to-defer tasks. This is a generalization of Neyman-Pearson lemma and counters the regularization paradigm."
    url="https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.12710"
  />
  <style>
    .glow-button {
        border: 1.5px solid black;
        /* padding: 10px; */
        background: white;
        color: black;
        transition: 0.3s;
    }
    .glow-button:hover {
        box-shadow: 0 0 10px black;
    }
</style>
  <a href="https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2024/file/2a5a41a536d3ada8fbf61a9d6fbf18d2-Paper-Conference.pdf" target="_blank">
    <button class="glow-button"> &nbsp; PDF &nbsp; </button>
</a>
</style>
<a href="https://github.com/AminChrs/PostProcess" target="_blank">
  <button class="glow-button"> &nbsp; Code &nbsp; </button>
</a>
<a href="https://github.com/charusaie/charusaie.github.io/tree/gh-pages/slides/Constrained_L2D.pdf" target="_blank">
  <button class="glow-button"> &nbsp; Slides &nbsp; </button>
</a>
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Sample Efficient Learning of Predictors that Complement Humans"
    img="/Eff.webp"
    desc="In here, we provide the first theoretical results on the joint learning of classifier and rejector, and design an active learning algorithm to achieve this. We further introduce a set of surrogate losses to enable learn-to-defer training for neural networks."
    url="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v162/charusaie22a/charusaie22a.pdf"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Hermite Polynomial Features for Private Data Generation"
    img="/DPHP.webp"
    desc="In this paper, we designed an alternative to random features to generate more efficient representations of a dataset that are privacy-preserving, while maintain the quality of the instances."
    url="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v162/vinaroz22a/vinaroz22a.pdf"
  />

  <div>
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold mb-5 mt-10">Information Theory</div>
  </div>

  <HorizontalCard
    title="ARMA Processes with Discrete-Continuous Excitation: Compressibility Beyond Sparsity"
    img="/webp2.webp"
    desc="In this paper, I generalize the connection between information dimension and compressibility of stochastic processes to the case of ARMA processes. I show that although ARMA processes are not sparse, they can have singular structures that lead to their compression via compressed sensing methods."
    url="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2406.06349.pdf"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="Compressibility Measures for Affinely Singular Random Vectors"
    img="/RDE.webp"
    desc="In this paper, we define a set of singular distributions that naturally arise in autoregressive processes. Then, we obtain R\'enyi information dimension for processes with such probability distributions. We further, find an extension to differential entropy for such class of probability measures. Then, we find information-theoretic and compressed sensing reconstruction errors for compression of samples of such processes."
    url="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.03884.pdf"
  />
  <div class="divider my-0"></div>
  <HorizontalCard
    title="On the Compressibility of Affinely Singular Random Vectors"
    img="/ASRV.webp"
    desc="In this paper, I find a probabilistic extension to sparsity that can lead to similar  guarantees in reconstruction error in compressed sensing problems. This is done by finding R\'enyi Information Dimension for probability measures with singularity."
    url="https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Mohammad-Amin-Charusaie/publication/343842135_On_the_Compressibility_of_Affinely_Singular_Random_Vectors/links/5f4d151d299bf13c5068a83f/On-the-Compressibility-of-Affinely-Singular-Random-Vectors.pdf"
  />
</BaseLayout>
